Gas Dynamics — Vinayak Kulkarni (@fd-gas-dynamics: 0, is #reference, #part-of @fd-sources) { r_34YGDV61X77JFYZH8X8NGDBS9W
Vinayak Kulkarni, IIT Guwahati. NPTEL Gas Dynamics, course 112103021. [Official course and lessons](https://nptel.ac.in/courses/112103021) · [Official syllabus](https://archive.nptel.ac.in/content/syllabus_pdf/112103021.pdf).

Study the full public progression from governing equations through one-dimensional shocks, Rayleigh and Fanno flow, oblique shocks and expansion, nozzles, linearized flows and characteristics, shock tubes, and experimental facilities. Reconstruct the equations and solve unfamiliar problems before comparing with the reference tables in [Equations, Tables, and Charts for Compressible Flow — NACA 1135](Compressible-Flow-NACA-1135.lingua#r_5V6PTWHXNJS515S6PMX7BN2ZHM).

The official indexed lessons and syllabus identify this as a web course. Preserve the distinctions among available written lessons, any linked media and current assessed offerings; no full video programme or completed assessment is asserted. Course material and cited commercial books retain their own notices. All source files remain external.

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics sources — books, courses, methods and physical evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_3Y3TVV9VQAB50M2ZSECK5JTYVG).
